      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>Are color prediction results actually predictable?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Not in a guaranteed way. Short streaks can happen naturally in random systems, which makes people think they found a pattern. The safer approach is to accept uncertainty and control your exposure: fewer rounds, fixed unit size, time limits, and breaks. Those habits reduce risky decisions more than any ‘secret trick’.</div></details>
<details><summary>What’s the safest way to start on a new platform?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Start slow. Verify the domain/app source, read basic rules and payout logic, and understand deposit/withdraw policies before putting money in. Then set a small budget and a short session timer. If you feel pressure to chase losses or ‘recover fast’, pause and stop for the day.</div></details>
<details><summary>Why do people lose money quickly in fast timer games?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Because speed creates impulsive decisions. People place more bets than planned, chase losses, and rely on tiny samples like the last 5 results. A single emotional session can erase many small wins. Limiting rounds per session and keeping bet size fixed are simple, effective protections.</div></details>
