      <h2 style="margin-top:26px">FAQs</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>What is a first deposit bonus?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>A first deposit bonus (welcome bonus) is a promotion where the platform adds extra balance/credits after your first deposit. It sounds simple, but the important part is the terms: wagering/turnover rules, validity days, max bet limits, and withdrawal caps. Before claiming, read the offer page and the bonus rules section so you know what is required and what is optional.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is a bonus the same as free money?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Usually no. Most bonuses are marketing offers with conditions. You might need to complete wagering, stay within certain bet limits, or use the bonus only in specific modes. A safe mindset is to treat the bonus as optional and deposit only what you can afford to lose, even if the promotion looks attractive.</div></details>
<details><summary>What does wagering or turnover mean?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Wagering/turnover is the total amount of bets you may need to place before bonus-linked funds can be withdrawn. Example: a 10x wagering rule can mean you must place bets totaling 10 times the bonus amount. Different platforms calculate this differently, so always check the exact wording on the offer and in the terms.</div></details>
<details><summary>Why do bonuses have max bet limits?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Max bet limits reduce abuse and keep risk within a range the platform is comfortable with. If you exceed the maximum bet size while a bonus is active, some platforms may remove the bonus or make bonus winnings ineligible. If you claim a bonus, keep your bet size fixed and below any listed caps.</div></details>
<details><summary>Can I withdraw right after the first deposit?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>It depends on the platform’s withdrawal policy. Some allow quick withdrawals, while others require verification (KYC), a minimum withdrawal amount, or a waiting period. The best move is to read the withdrawal section before depositing, so you don’t get surprised later when you need funds.</div></details>
<details><summary>How do I avoid surprises with bonus terms?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Take 2 minutes to do three checks: (1) read validity (how long the bonus lasts), (2) read wagering requirements, and (3) read max withdrawal or game restrictions. If anything is unclear or hidden, skip the bonus. Clear rules are a sign of a healthier user experience.</div></details>
<details><summary>Should I increase my betting to clear wagering faster?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>No—this is one of the most common mistakes. Increasing bet size to clear wagering can raise losses quickly. A safer approach is to keep a fixed, small unit size, set a time limit, and stop when you reach your planned budget. Clearing wagering is never worth breaking your limits.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do promotions change over time?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Yes, promotions can change. A platform might update the bonus amount, eligibility, or terms. If you are returning after a few weeks, re-check the offer details before depositing. Saving a screenshot of the rules can also help you remember what you agreed to.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it okay to play without any bonus?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Absolutely. Many users have a better experience when they ignore promotions and stick to a simple budget. Playing without a bonus keeps the rules simpler and reduces pressure to “complete wagering.” If you choose a bonus, choose only one that fits your normal plan.</div></details>
<details><summary>What’s the safest way to use a first deposit bonus?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Use it only if the rules are clear and the deposit amount is within your comfort zone. Keep fixed bet sizes, use a strict session timer, and stop if you feel emotional or pressured. The goal is to stay in control and avoid treating a bonus as a promise of profit.</div></details>
