        <details><summary>Are color prediction results actually predictable?</summary><div class='muted' style='margin-top:8px'>Not in a guaranteed way. Short streaks can happen naturally in random systems, which makes people think they found a pattern. The safer approach is to accept uncertainty and control your exposure: fewer rounds, fixed unit size, time limits, and breaks. Those habits reduce risky decisions more than any ‘secret trick’.</div></details>
